    "text": "Disease: Rice Blast (Blast Disease)\nTamil Name: நெல் வெடிப்பு நோய்\nHindi Name: धान का झुलसा रोग\nCrop: Rice\nPathogen: Magnaporthe oryzae\n\nSymptoms:\n• Diamond-shaped lesions with gray centers and brown margins on leaves\n• Whitish-gray spots with brown edges\n• Leaf blast - small brown spots that enlarge\n• Neck blast - blackening of neck region causing panicle to fall\n• Node blast - blackening of nodes\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Neem oil spray @ 5ml/liter water\n• Pseudomonas fluorescens @ 10g/liter spray\n• Trichoderma viride seed treatment and foliar spray\n• Remove and destroy infected plant parts\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Tricyclazole 75% WP @ 0.6g/liter water\n• Carbendazim 50% WP @ 1g/liter\n• Isoprothiolane 40% EC @ 1.5ml/liter\n• Spray at tillering, booting, and flowering stages\n\nPrevention:\n• Use resistant varieties like IR-64, Jaya, Swarna\n• Balanced fertilization - avoid excess nitrogen\n• Proper water management\n• Seed treatment with Carbendazim\n• Maintain field hygiene\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
