    "text": "Disease: Sheath Blight\nTamil Name: உறை எரிப்பு நோய்\nHindi Name: म्यान झुलसा\nCrop: Rice\nPathogen: Rhizoctonia solani\n\nSymptoms:\n• Greenish-gray oval lesions on leaf sheath near water level\n• Spots with brown margins and white centers\n• Lesions coalesce and move upward\n• Snake-skin pattern on stems\n• Affected tillers turn yellow and die\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Pseudomonas fluorescens @ 2.5kg/ha mixed in FYM\n• Neem cake @ 250kg/ha\n• Trichoderma harzianum soil application\n• Maintain proper water level\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Validamycin 3% L @ 2.5ml/liter\n• Hexaconazole 5% SC @ 2ml/liter\n• Propiconazole 25% EC @ 1ml/liter\n• Spray twice at flowering stage\n\nPrevention:\n• Avoid excess nitrogen fertilization\n• Proper plant spacing\n• Drain water periodically\n• Use balanced fertilizer\n• Remove crop residues\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
