    "text": "Disease: Tungro Disease (Yellow Spots)\nTamil Name: துங்க்ரோ நோய்\nHindi Name: टंगरो रोग\nCrop: Rice\nPathogen: Rice tungro virus (transmitted by green leafhoppers)\n\nSymptoms:\n• Yellow or orange-yellow discoloration of leaves\n• Yellow spots and streaks on leaves\n• Stunted growth and reduced tillering\n• Delayed flowering\n• Mottled and twisted leaves\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Control green leafhopper vectors with neem spray\n• Remove and destroy infected plants immediately\n• Use yellow sticky traps for leafhopper control\n• Neem oil @ 5ml/liter + soap solution\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• No direct cure - focus on vector control\n• Imidacloprid 17.8% SL @ 0.3ml/liter for leafhopper control\n• Thiamethoxam 25% WG @ 0.2g/liter\n• Spray at early tillering stage\n\nPrevention:\n• Plant resistant varieties like TKM-6, Vikram\n• Control green leafhoppers\n• Avoid staggered planting\n• Roguing of infected plants\n• Use virus-free seeds\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
