    "text": "Disease: Early Blight\nTamil Name: ஆரம்ப எரிப்பு\nHindi Name: आरंभिक अंगमारी\nCrop: Tomato\nPathogen: Alternaria solani\n\nSymptoms:\n• Dark brown spots with concentric rings (target board pattern)\n• Yellowing around spots\n• Lower leaves affected first\n• Premature leaf drop\n• Stem lesions with similar pattern\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Copper fungicide spray @ 3g/liter\n• Baking soda solution @ 5g/liter + soap\n• Neem oil @ 10ml/liter\n• Remove infected lower leaves\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Mancozeb 75% WP @ 2.5g/liter\n• Chlorothalonil 75% WP @ 2g/liter\n• Difenoconazole 25% EC @ 1ml/liter\n• Spray every 7-10 days\n\nPrevention:\n• Crop rotation with non-solanaceous crops\n• Stake plants for air circulation\n• Mulching to prevent soil splash\n• Drip irrigation instead of overhead\n• Remove crop debris\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
