    "text": "Disease: Cotton Wilt\nTamil Name: பருத்தி வாடல்\nHindi Name: कपास म्लानि\nCrop: Cotton\nPathogen: Fusarium oxysporum f.sp. vasinfectum\n\nSymptoms:\n• Yellowing and drooping of leaves\n• Wilting of entire plant\n• Brown discoloration of vascular tissue\n• One-sided wilting common\n• Stunted growth\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Trichoderma viride seed treatment @ 10g/kg seed\n• Soil application of Pseudomonas @ 2.5kg/ha\n• Neem cake @ 500kg/ha\n• No cure once infected - focus on prevention\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Carbendazim 50% WP @ 2g/kg seed treatment\n• Soil drenching with Carbendazim @ 2g/liter\n• Metalaxyl + Mancozeb soil drench\n\nPrevention:\n• Plant resistant varieties like Bunny Bt, RCH-2\n• Crop rotation with cereals\n• Deep summer ploughing\n• Balanced fertilization\n• Avoid waterlogging\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
