    "text": "Disease: Chilli Leaf Curl\nTamil Name: மிளகாய் இலை சுருட்டல்\nHindi Name: मिर्च पत्ती मोड़\nCrop: Chilli\nPathogen: Chilli leaf curl virus (transmitted by whitefly)\n\nSymptoms:\n• Upward curling of leaves\n• Yellowing and puckering of leaves\n• Stunted plant growth\n• Reduced flowering and fruiting\n• Small and distorted fruits\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Control whiteflies with neem oil @ 5ml/liter\n• Yellow sticky traps for whitefly monitoring\n• Remove and destroy infected plants\n• Spray neem + soap solution weekly\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Imidacloprid 17.8% SL @ 0.5ml/liter for whitefly control\n• Thiamethoxam 25% WG @ 0.2g/liter\n• Acetamiprid 20% SP @ 0.2g/liter\n• Spray at 10-day intervals\n\nPrevention:\n• Plant resistant varieties\n• Control whitefly population\n• Remove infected plants immediately\n• Mulching with silver plastic\n• Avoid mixed cropping with cucurbits\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
