    "text": "Disease: Panama Wilt (Fusarium Wilt)\nTamil Name: வாழை வாடல் நோய்\nHindi Name: केला मुरझान\nCrop: Banana\nPathogen: Fusarium oxysporum f.sp. cubense\n\nSymptoms:\n• Yellowing of older leaves first\n• Splitting of leaf sheaths\n• Wilting and drooping of leaves\n• Brown discoloration of pseudostem\n• Plant death within weeks\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• No cure - remove infected plants\n• Soil solarization\n• Trichoderma application @ 5kg/ha\n• Organic matter addition\n• Crop rotation impossible as banana is perennial\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Carbendazim soil drench @ 2g/liter\n• Propiconazole @ 1ml/liter soil drench\n• Preventive only - no cure once infected\n\nPrevention:\n• Plant disease-free suckers\n• Use tissue culture plants\n• Plant resistant varieties like Dwarf Cavendish\n• Avoid waterlogging\n• Quarantine infected areas\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
