    "text": "Disease: Wheat Rust (Brown/Yellow Rust)\nTamil Name: கோதுமை துருப்பிடிப்பு\nHindi Name: गेहूं का रतुआ\nCrop: Wheat\nPathogen: Puccinia triticina (brown rust), P. striiformis (yellow rust)\n\nSymptoms:\n• Orange-brown pustules on leaves (brown rust)\n• Yellow stripes on leaves (yellow rust)\n• Premature leaf drying\n• Reduced grain filling\n• Black pustules at maturity\n\nOrganic Treatment:\n• Sulfur dust @ 20kg/ha\n• Copper oxychloride @ 3g/liter spray\n• Remove alternate hosts (barberry)\n• Early sowing to escape disease\n\nChemical Treatment:\n• Propiconazole 25% EC @ 1ml/liter\n• Tebuconazole 25% EC @ 1ml/liter\n• Mancozeb + Carbendazim @ 2g/liter\n• Spray at first sign of disease\n\nPrevention:\n• Plant resistant varieties like HD-2967, PBW-343\n• Early sowing (October-November)\n• Avoid excess nitrogen\n• Timely irrigation\n• Destroy crop residues\n\nFavorable Conditions:\nNot specified\n\nIntegrated Pest Management:\nNot specified",
